      "side": 1,
      "message": "Both record types look like fixed-size SEL records: the offsets the handlers use match the 16-byte IPMI SEL record layout that fb-ipmi-oem defines for both (StdSELEntry and NtsOemSELEntry), without its 2-byte record ID (eventData[8] is the sensor type, eventData[11..13] are event data 1-3). I did not find a PLDM-side description of the payload, so that rests on the offsets matching. I also ran a harness that links the real oem_event_manager.cpp with the buffer against a guard page: without the check, a 13-byte payload faults in the handler reads for both record types and a 14-byte one does not; with it, anything shorter than 14 bytes is rejected. On that basis a per-type check would use 14 for both types handled today; a new record type would need its own size. The commit message has the same explanation, and there is a comment at the constant.",
